## 💪 Stress Test Plan

### Stress Test 1: Rapid Allocation & Deallocation
```
Scenario: Allocate and free objects rapidly
Parameters:
  - Iterations: 10,000
  - Array sizes: 10-1,000 elements
  - GC trigger frequency: Every 100 allocations

Expected Results:
  - No memory leaks
  - No corruption
  - GC pause time < 10ms
  - Fragmentation stabilizes < 10%
```

**Pseudo-code**:
```rust
#[test]
fn stress_test_rapid_allocation() {
    let mut gc = GarbageCollector::new();
    let mut stack = vec![0; 5000];
    let mut globals = vec![0; 100];

    for i in 0..10_000 {
        // Allocate
        gc.register_allocation(0x5000 + (i * 10), 10, ObjectType::Array(5));

        // Every 100 allocations, trigger GC
        if i % 100 == 0 {
            gc.collect(&stack[..], &globals[..]);
        }
    }

    // Final verification
    assert!(gc.allocated_objects_count() < 100); // Most freed
    assert!(gc.fragmentation_ratio() < 0.10);
    assert_eq!(gc.collections, 100); // 10,000 / 100
}
```

