## ⚡ Benchmark Specifications

### Benchmark 1: Allocation Performance
```
Measure: Time to allocate N objects
Parameters:
  - N values: 100, 1,000, 10,000, 100,000
  - Object sizes: 8, 64, 512 bytes
  - Allocator: BumpPointer (after compaction)

Expected Results:
  - Constant O(1) time regardless of N
  - BumpPointer: ~10-20 nanoseconds per allocation
  - No O(n) search overhead
```

### Benchmark 2: Mark-Sweep Performance
```
Measure: GC cycle time vs. object count
Parameters:
  - Object counts: 100, 1,000, 10,000
  - Reachability: 50%, 75%, 90%
  - Object types: Arrays (50%), Strings (50%)

Expected Results:
  - Linear O(n) scaling
  - Mark phase: ~0.5µs per object
  - Sweep phase: ~0.3µs per object
  - Total: ~0.8µs per object

Example:
  - 1,000 objects: ~0.8ms
  - 10,000 objects: ~8ms
  - 100,000 objects: ~80ms
```

### Benchmark 3: Compaction Performance
```
Measure: LISP2 compaction time vs. fragmentation
Parameters:
  - Object counts: 100, 1,000, 10,000
  - Fragmentation: 10%, 20%, 30%
  - Pass 1 (calculate): O(n)
  - Pass 2 (update refs): O(n)

Expected Results:
  - Linear O(n) scaling (both passes)
  - LISP2 overhead: ~2µs per object
  - 1,000 objects: ~2ms
  - 10,000 objects: ~20ms

Real-world fragmentation impact:
  Before: 28KB heap, 20% wasted = 5.6KB
  After: 28KB heap, <5% wasted = 1.4KB
  Improvement: 3-4x memory efficiency
```

### Benchmark 4: Stack Operations
```
Measure: Time per stack operation
Operations:
  - PUSH: ~10ns (simple increment)
  - POP: ~10ns (simple decrement)
  - DUP: ~20ns (copy value)
  - SWAP: ~30ns (exchange two values)

Expected:
  - Negligible compared to GC
  - 100x faster than allocation
```

### Benchmark 5: Overall VM Throughput
```
Measure: Instructions executed per second (IPS)
Program: Simple arithmetic loop
  PUSH 0
  STORE 0      # i = 0
LOOP:
  LOAD 0       # Load i
  PUSH 1
  ADD          # i++
  STORE 0      # Store i
  PUSH 100
  LT           # i < 100?
  JIT LOOP
  PUSH 1
  HALT

Expected:
  - ~100,000 IPS (100K instructions/second)
  - Includes GC pauses
  - Dominated by instruction dispatch overhead
```

